description:
FILED s532c (Opus agent, 2026-11-08): the reduction of #4221's t/dom.t `*PLAN*` row (the file dies "Not an ARRAY reference" after row 8).

WHERE: t/dom.t:217 `is $dom->[0]->type, 'doctype', 'right type';` -- the 40th assertion of subtest 'Nodes' (the 39 before it pass; PCL then prints `ok 8 - Nodes` and dies, exactly as perl does for a dying subtest body -- probe scratch/s532c/p/4221-12.pl).  Mojo::DOM58 is a blessed SCALAR reference with
  use overload '@{}' => sub { shift->child_nodes }, '%{}' => sub { shift->attr }, bool => sub {1}, '""' => sub { shift->to_string }, fallback => 1;
and the rest of t/dom.t uses `$dom->[i]` / `$dom->{attr}` throughout, so every row after 'Nodes' 39 sits behind this one mechanism.  Backtrace: scratch/s532c/p/dom-bt.out (the raise is %p-not-a-ref directly in the subtest's anon sub).

MINIMAL REPRODUCER (scratch/s532c/p/4221-10.pl; perl 5.40.3):
  package Obj;
  use overload '@{}' => sub { $_[0]->kids }, '%{}' => sub { {a=>7} }, '""' => sub { "OBJ" }, fallback => 1;
  sub new { my ($c) = @_; my $s = \my $x; bless $s, $c }
  sub kids { ['k0', 'k1'] }
  package main;
  my $o = Obj->new;
  print "A ", $o->[0], "\n"; print "B ", $o->[1], "\n"; print "C ", scalar(@$o), "\n";
  print "D ", $$o[0], "\n"; print "E ", $o->{a}, "\n"; my @l = @{$o}; print "F @l\n";
perl: A k0 / B k1 / C 2 / D k0 / E 7 / F k0 k1.   PCL (main ce665621 and s532c's tree): dies "Not an ARRAY reference" at the first line.
Referent variants (4221-10a.pl: the object is a blessed ARRAY [9]; 4221-10h.pl: a blessed HASH): perl answers through the handler in BOTH (A k0 even though the referent IS an array -- perl consults `@{}` on every array dereference of an object whose class overloads it; a handler that returns the object itself gets the native dereference).  PCL: the array object reads its own element (A 9, C 1 -- SILENT WRONG) and then dies "Not a HASH reference" at E; the hash object dies at A.

MECHANISM: #3395 implemented the CODE dereference overload `&{}` (p-funcall-ref's not-a-function branch) and wrote "NOT done: the other dereference overloads `@{}` `%{}` `${}` `*{}`".  This is that residue.  The array/hash dereference has many entry points in cl/pcl-runtime.lisp (13 `(%p-not-a-ref "ARRAY")` + 14 `(%p-not-a-ref "HASH")` raise sites: element read/write, flatten, scalar(@$x), $#$x, slices, exists/delete, keys/values/each, push/pop/shift/unshift/splice) -- so it is NOT a one-site fix.  Shape to measure first: ONE resolver `%p-deref-overload (value kind)` asked at each site's off-fast-path arm (a blessed value whose class has the handler -> the handler's answer, re-dispatched; the handler returning the object itself -> the native referent), plus the decision whether the ON-path case (an array/hash object whose class overloads `@{}`/`%{}`) is taken (it needs a per-class "has deref overload" bit so the fast path stays a type test -- the #1040-style cost question; measure on the bench).  Rule 12: a handler answering a non-reference dies perl's way ("Overloaded dereference did not return a reference").
BOARD: Mojo-DOM58 t/dom.t `*PLAN*` re-keyed to this task (was UNREDUCED #4221).  Not fixed in s532c: a runtime-wide change outside a resume's scope.
